'\" t
.TH DVBTX-CHANNEL 1 2026-11-02 "dvbtx 0.1.0" "dvbtx manual"
.SH NAME
dvbtx\-channel \- list, add, remove, rename, renumber channels and change their source while dvbtx is on air
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
dvbtx channel [\-c FILE] [\-\-url URL] [\-\-token TOKEN] [\-\-offline] COMMAND ...

dvbtx channel list [\-\-json]
dvbtx channel add NAME SOURCE... [\-\-number N] [\-\-mux MUX] [\-\-sid SID] [\-\-backup SRC | \-\-no\-backup]
                                 [\-\-cache MS|auto] [\-\-option KEY=VALUE]...
dvbtx channel remove CHANNEL
dvbtx channel rename CHANNEL NEW_NAME
dvbtx channel renumber CHANNEL NUMBER [\-\-swap]
dvbtx channel source CHANNEL SOURCE... [\-\-backup SRC | \-\-no\-backup] [\-\-cache MS|auto] [\-\-option KEY=VALUE]...
dvbtx channel set CHANNEL KEY=VALUE...
.EE
.PP
\fBchannels\fR is accepted for \fBchannel\fR, \fBrm\fR and \fBdelete\fR for \fBremove\fR. The common options may be
given before or after the command.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
A channel is a service of a multiplex (a \fB[[carrier.service]]\fR of the configuration). While dvbtx
runs, \fBdvbtx channel\fR sends the change to it through its web API (\fBweb.listen\fR): the change is
applied at once to that channel only, and written back to the configuration file, so that the next
start gives the same channels. The other channels of the multiplex, and the other multiplexes, are
not interrupted: no packet lost, no extra delay (measured: the longest gap between two video packets
of a neighbouring channel stays at 25\-33 ms, as without change).
.PP
When nothing answers on the web address, dvbtx is not running: the configuration file alone is
edited, and the change is applied at the next start (or at once with \fBsystemctl reload dvbtx\fR if it
was in fact running with its web page disabled).
.PP
\fBCHANNEL\fR designates a channel by its number (LCN: \fB5\fR), its service_id (\fB0x0105\fR, \fBsid:261\fR) or
its name (\fB"France 24"\fR, any case; a name made of digits is taken as a number).
.SS What each change does on air
.PP
.TS
allbox tab(@);
lb lb
l lx.
change@on air
\fBadd\fR@T{
new service in the PAT (new version), SDT, NIT (number), EIT; its source starts, the backup plays meanwhile (after \fBswitch_timeout_ms\fR)
T}
\fBremove\fR@T{
out of the PAT, SDT, NIT, EIT; its source is stopped (a backup shared with other channels is kept)
T}
\fBrename\fR@T{
SDT (the TV shows the new name at its next scan of the SDT, usually within seconds)
T}
\fBrenumber\fR@T{
NIT logical_channel_descriptor (most TVs only reorder at a new channel scan)
T}
\fBsource\fR@T{
\fBno cut\fR: the new source starts beside the old one; the channel switches to it on a video key frame due at that moment (or, without video, as soon as it has data due), the old source plays until then (15 s at most, then the channel goes on as usual: its backup if the new source does not come)
T}
\fB\-\-backup\fR@T{
the new backup is used from the next failure of the source (at once if the channel is on its backup)
T}
\fBset\fR@T{
any other service setting: a setting of the source (\fBytdlp_format\fR, \fBencode\fR, \fBreadrate\fR, \fBmap\fR...) restarts the source like \fBsource\fR (no cut); an engine setting (\fBswitch_timeout_ms\fR, \fBreturn_ms\fR, \fBmax_late_ms\fR, \fBearly_ms\fR, \fBpcr_max_ms\fR, \fBpmt_period_ms\fR, \fBpriority\fR, \fBpid_base\fR) re\-creates the service (cut of a few seconds)
T}
.TE
.PP
The service_id and the multiplex of a channel cannot be changed: remove it and add it again.
.SS Several sources, in order of preference
.PP
Several \fBSOURCE\fRs (a TOML list in the file: \fBsource = ["first", "second", ...]\fR, one per line on
the web page, a JSON list in the API), as many as needed. The first one plays. When the source
playing has delivered nothing for \fBfailover_s\fR (10 s), or has not started within \fBsource_start_s\fR
(30 s), it is stopped and the next one started (after the last, the first again); the channel plays
its backup meanwhile. A source is also left when it is unstable: the channel fell back to its
backup \fBunstable_switches\fR times (3) within \fBunstable_window_s\fR (600 s), or stayed on it
\fBfailover_s\fR + \fBreturn_ms\fR (20 s). A source left is tried again later each time (5 min, then 10,
20... up to an hour), forgiven once it has held 30 min. While not on the first one, the preferred ones are tried again, in order,
every \fBpreferred_retry_s\fR (300 s; 0: never), beside the one playing: as soon as one delivers for
2 s, the channel goes back to it without a cut. When none works, the backup clip (\fBbackup\fR) plays.
\fBlist\fR, the web page and the alerts say which one plays (\fB*2\fR, \fBsource 2/3\fR).
.PP
A failed source is stopped before the next one starts, so an IPTV account allowing one connection
can be given several of its streams. Trying a preferred source while another plays opens a second
connection for a few seconds (start, 2 s of stream, the switch, then the other is closed): most
accounts tolerate it, as when zapping; otherwise the provider refuses it (nothing changes) or drops
the other (a few seconds of backup, then the preferred one); \fBpreferred_retry_s = 0\fR avoids these
trials.
.SS Cache
.PP
\fB\-\-cache MS\fR (\fBbuffer_ms\fR, 100 to 30000) is the delay accepted between the arrival of the source and
its transmission. Larger, an irregular source goes through without lost packets nor switch to the
backup, the channel being later than live. \fBauto\fR (default): 6000 ms for sources delivered in
segments (YouTube, Twitch, \fB.m3u8\fR: at the live edge of the playlist they arrive in bursts, one per
segment of 2 to 5 s), 1000 ms otherwise. A source is only taken as down once its cache has played
out. A change of cache restarts the source beside the old one (no cut).
.SS Numbers, service_id and PIDs stay where they are
.PP
By default the service_id, the number and the PIDs of a channel follow its position in the file.
TVs identify a channel by its service_id: a removal must not shift the others. So every structural
change (\fBadd\fR, \fBremove\fR, \fBrenumber\fR) writes \fBsid\fR, \fBlcn\fR and \fBpid_base\fR explicitly in the services
of the file that relied on the defaults. A new channel takes the first free service_id of its
multiplex (TSID × 256 + n), the first free number and the first free PID range (32 PIDs from 0x100).
.SS The configuration file
.PP
Only the \fB[[carrier.service]]\fR blocks concerned are rewritten; comments and layout of the rest are
kept, the previous version is kept as \fBFILE.bak\fR, and the result is read back: if it does not say
exactly what was meant (unusual layout, such as a setting given in a \fB[carrier.service.encode]\fR
sub\-table changed into another form), the file is left as it was and the change is only live
(\fBwarning: not saved ...\fR).
.PP
The file is not written when it differs from what is running (edited by hand meanwhile: apply your
edit first with \fBsystemctl reload dvbtx\fR), or when the channels come from the command line
(\fB\-\-service\fR, \fB\-\-set carrier.N.service...\fR).
.SS Editing the file by hand
.PP
\fBsystemctl reload dvbtx\fR (SIGHUP) re\-reads the file and applies the differences of the channels in
the same way, channel by channel (the EPG and SI tables are re\-read too). Changes of the radios or
multiplexes need a restart (logged, channels then left as they are); other settings outside the
channels are logged as needing a restart. Give \fBsid\fR explicitly to the channels you move or remove
by hand, or the following ones change service_id.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBlist [\-\-json]\fR
the channels: number, service_id, name, multiplex, what is on air (\fBprimary\fR, \fBbackup\fR, \fBnone\fR),
source and backup. From the file when dvbtx is not running.
.TP
\fBadd NAME SOURCE...\fR
\fBSOURCE\fR is any source dvbtx reads (several: in order of preference, see above) (file, \fBdir:\fR, URL, HLS, \fBytdlp:\fR, \fBtwitch://\fR, \fBm3u:\fR,
\fBudp://\fR, \fBrtmp://\fR, \fBsrt://\fR, \fBv4l2:\fR, \fBlavfi:\fR...). \fB\-\-number N\fR (default: the first free one),
\fB\-\-mux MUX\fR (index or name of the multiplex; required when there are several), \fB\-\-sid SID\fR,
\fB\-\-backup SRC\fR (default: \fBdefaults.backup\fR) or \fB\-\-no\-backup\fR, \fB\-\-option KEY=VALUE\fR for any
service setting (repeatable; values as in TOML: \fBencode=true\fR, \fBytdlp_format=b\fR, \fBpriority=7\fR).
.TP
\fBremove CHANNEL\fR
removes the channel.
.TP
\fBrename CHANNEL NEW_NAME\fR
1 to 60 characters, no quotes or backslashes.
.TP
\fBrenumber CHANNEL NUMBER [\-\-swap]\fR
refused if the number is taken, unless \fB\-\-swap\fR: the other channel then gets the old number.
.TP
\fBsource CHANNEL SOURCE... [\-\-backup SRC | \-\-no\-backup] [\-\-cache MS|auto] [\-\-option KEY=VALUE]...\fR
plays another source (or list of sources) on the channel without cutting it. \fB\-\-option\fR sets the service settings
that go with the new source (\fBKEY=\fR with nothing removes one, e.g. a \fBytdlp_format\fR that does not
apply to the new source).
.TP
\fBset CHANNEL KEY=VALUE...\fR
changes any setting of the channel (\fBKEY=\fR removes it, back to the default).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-config FILE\fR
configuration file (default \fB/etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml\fR): its \fBweb.listen\fR and \fBweb.token\fR are used
to reach the running dvbtx, and it is the file edited when dvbtx is not running.
.TP
\fB\-\-url URL\fR
web address of the running dvbtx (default \fBhttp://\fR + \fBweb.listen\fR, \fB0.0.0.0\fR read as
\fB127.0.0.1\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-token TOKEN\fR
\fBweb.token\fR of the running dvbtx (also \fBDVBTX_TOKEN\fR in the environment).
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
edit the configuration file only, even if dvbtx is running (to prepare several changes, then
\fBsystemctl reload dvbtx\fR).
.SH WEB PAGE AND API
.PP
The web page has a \fB+ Ajouter une chaîne\fR button per multiplex and \fBModifier\fR / \fB✕\fR buttons
per channel (name, number with swap, sources, cache, backup); the result of each change is shown, and
whether it was written to the file.
.PP
.EX
GET    /api/channels                  [{"lcn", "sid", "name", "source", "backup", "carrier", "on", ...}]
POST   /api/channels                  {"name", "source", "carrier"?, "lcn"?, "sid"?, "backup"?, options...}
PATCH  /api/channels/<channel>        {"name"?, "lcn"?, "swap"?, "source"?, "backup"?, "buffer_ms"?, options...}
DELETE /api/channels/<channel>
.EE
.PP
\fB<channel>\fR as CHANNEL above, URL\-encoded. \fB"source"\fR: a string or a list (in order of
preference); \fB"buffer_ms": null\fR back to auto. \fB"backup": ""\fR (or \fBfalse\fR) removes the backup, an option
set to \fBnull\fR is removed. Answer `{"ok": true, "sid", "changes": [text], "detail": [{"what", "name",
"from", "to"}], "saved", "warning"?}\fB, or \fR{"ok": false, "error"}` with status 400 (403, 401, 415:
see below).
.SH SECURITY
.PP
The web API can change what is broadcast, so:
.IP \(bu 2
requests that change something are refused when they come from another web site (\fBOrigin\fR
checked: a page you visit cannot drive the transmitter through your browser) and must send JSON
(\fBContent\-Type: application/json\fR);
.IP \(bu 2
\fBweb.token = "..."\fR: these requests then need \fBAuthorization: Bearer <token>\fR (the page asks for
it once, \fBdvbtx channel\fR reads it from the configuration file or \fB\-\-token\fR). Set one when
\fBweb.listen\fR is not \fB127.0.0.1\fR;
.IP \(bu 2
sources that run a command or read the standard input (\fBexec:\fR, \fBpipe:\fR, \fBstdin:\fR), and the raw
ffmpeg arguments \fBffmpeg_input\fR / \fBffmpeg_output\fR (they can name an output file), are refused
from the API unless \fBweb.allow_exec_sources = true\fR; they stay possible in the file.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB/etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml\fR
configuration, rewritten by the changes (it is a conffile of the package: an upgrade that brings
a new version of it asks what to do, as for any edit).
.TP
\fB/etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml.bak\fR
the version before the last change.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.EX
dvbtx channel list
dvbtx channel add "France 24" "http://provider.example/live/user/pass/976" \-\-number 3
dvbtx channel add "Sky News" "ytdlp:https://www.youtube.com/@SkyNews/live" \e
      \-\-option 'ytdlp_format=bv*[vcodec^=avc1][height<=720]+ba/b[height<=720]'
dvbtx channel source "Sky News" "https://example.org/sky/index.m3u8" \-\-option ytdlp_format=
dvbtx channel source "France 24" http://provider.example/u/p/289 http://provider.example/u/p/319 \e
      http://provider.example/u/p/976          # FHD, then HD, then Caribbean, then the backup clip
dvbtx channel source "Seismic" twitch://dynamicearthcommunitylive \-\-cache 8000
dvbtx channel rename 3 "France 24 FR"
dvbtx channel renumber "France 24 FR" 1 \-\-swap
dvbtx channel set 3 epg_id=France24.fr
dvbtx channel remove 0x0103
dvbtx channel \-\-offline \-c /etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml add "Mire" lavfi:smptehdbars && sudo systemctl reload dvbtx
curl \-s \-X PATCH \-H 'Content\-Type: application/json' \-d '{"name": "Info"}' http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/channels/3
.EE
